From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:43:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Sentinel: a protocol switch never parks the calling thread

Connection#setupInboundProtocol and #setupOutboundProtocol waited with
syncUninterruptibly for the channel loop to swap the decoder or the encoder.
Called from the server thread (configuration -> play, play -> configuration,
login -> configuration), one saturated or stalled loop froze the whole
server: a wave of 50 connections gave an 8.7 s MSPT and two watchdogs.

The switch is a task in the loop's single FIFO queue, ahead of every packet
sent after it (sendPacket queues from off-loop threads), and inbound reads
stay off until the decoder swap runs, so the order holds without waiting.
The outcome is now observed with a listener: a closed channel is logged at
info as before, any other failure is logged and disconnects the connection.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index cd1ae64448fec64dc8956c3fdd2344a37866cc26..93eea2618597ccb2534f53a2b4217135f8cb8895 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -312,17 +312,17 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
         }
     }
 
-    private static void syncAfterConfigurationChange(final ChannelFuture future) {
-        try {
-            future.syncUninterruptibly();
-        } catch (Exception e) {
-            if (e instanceof ClosedChannelException) {
-                LOGGER.info("Connection closed during protocol change");
-            } else {
-                throw e;
-            }
-        }
+    // BTCCore start - Sentinel: a protocol switch never parks the calling thread on the Netty loop
+    private void syncAfterConfigurationChange(final ChannelFuture future) {
+        // The switch is a task in the channel loop's single FIFO queue, ahead of every packet the caller sends after it
+        // (sendPacket queues from off-loop threads too), so encoder order holds without waiting; inbound stays at autoRead
+        // false until the decoder swap runs.
+        dev.btc.core.security.exploit.ProtocolSwitches.watch(future, cause -> {
+            LOGGER.error("Protocol change failed, disconnecting", cause);
+            this.disconnect(Component.translatable("disconnect.genericReason", "Internal Exception: " + cause));
+        });
     }
+    // BTCCore end - Sentinel: a protocol switch never parks the calling thread on the Netty loop
 
     public <T extends PacketListener> void setupInboundProtocol(final ProtocolInfo<T> protocol, final T packetListener) {
         this.validateListener(protocol, packetListener);
